REM applies the rest of a sequence after a traversal to the wrong term:
its generated code (StrategyTraversalAll.java) leaves v0, the term the next
strategy reads, at the result of the last argument instead of the rebuilt
term (REM prints o here). elanc-go applies the rest to the result of the
traversal (S7d plan, Task 6 rulings): g(s(o),s(s(o))).
